Would you like to contribute to flawless mail delivery and are you looking for a flexible part-time job? Become a mail preparer at our client in Assen! In this role, you will be responsible for ensuring that mail is correctly sorted and prepared for dispatch.

As a mail preparer in Assen, you are responsible for accurately sorting incoming mail. You will check addresses and shipping details and use various mail processing machines to handle the mail efficiently. The job requires precision and good physical condition, as you will be working primarily on your feet. You should also be open to working overtime to assist your colleagues during backlogs or busy periods.

What we ask for:

- No minimum educational requirements;
- Precision and attention to detail;
- Enthusiastic and motivated attitude;
- You speak either Dutch or English;
- Availability for 3 days, between Monday to Thursday.

Are you technically minded and looking for a challenging role in an innovative high-tech environment? Then this position as a VAS Technician could be the perfect opportunity for you!

You will work alongside a team of technicians and specialists, assembling, testing, and configuring advanced equipment. No two days are the same, and you will have plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills. In this role, you will be responsible for assembling, installing, and preparing technical equipment according to customer requirements. You will ensure that all products meet the required quality standards before they are shipped or installed.

Your responsibilities include:

- Assembling equipment and network setups according to instructions and customer requirements;
- Unpacking, preparing, and installing technical equipment;
- Performing quality inspections and technical verification activities;
- Identifying and reporting technical issues during assembly, testing, and installation processes;
- Following work instructions accurately and processing documentation correctly;
- Supporting installation, configuration, and disassembly activities;
- Maintaining a safe working environment at all times;
- Collaborating with colleagues and technical specialists to achieve project objectives;
- Participating in training programs to further develop your technical knowledge and skills.

You have a technical background and are motivated to further develop yourself within a high-tech environment. In addition, you recognize yourself in the following:

- You have completed a technical education at a minimum of MBO Level 4 or equivalent;
- You have a good command of the English language, at least B2 level;
- You are eager to learn and have an affinity for technology;
- Experience within a logistics or production environment is an advantage but not required;
- You are flexible and enjoy working as part of a team;
